-- R1 row 4 of specs/todo/PATTERN-REFERENCE-RULE-SPEC.md: the ONE carve-out.
--
-- A name that resolves only to a record SELECTOR still binds a fresh
-- wildcard. `Pay Alice `Ms Ng` amount` names the slot it is filling, which is
-- the established idiom — the memo found 26 corpus sites of this spelling and
-- every one is a deliberate wildcard, usually narrowed afterwards by PROVIDED.
-- A selector is a function and can never be the intended value in an action
-- slot, so nothing is lost by carving it out, and R3's claim that dropping
-- EXACTLY is always meaning-preserving depends on it.
--
-- The traces show the wildcard still matching any amount, and PROVIDED still
-- narrowing it: the first pays 1 and IS accepted by the bare wildcard, the
-- second is refused by the guarded rule until the amount is at least 1000.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Alice
    `Ms Ng`

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay HAS payer IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`any amount will do` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST Pay Alice `Ms Ng` amount WITHIN 30 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH

#TRACE `any amount will do` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES Pay Alice `Ms Ng` 1 AT 10

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`at least a thousand` MEANS
    PARTY Alice
    MUST Pay Alice `Ms Ng` amount PROVIDED amount AT LEAST 1000
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `at least a thousand` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES Pay Alice `Ms Ng` 1 AT 10
#TRACE `at least a thousand` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES Pay Alice `Ms Ng` 1000 AT 10
